sx';\n\n\n\n## Featur"},"328":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap-28","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap#examples","content":"import { ArgTypes, Meta } from '@storybook/addon-docs/blocks';\nimport { Examples } from '@bento/storybook-addon-helpers/runtime';\nimport * as Stories from './heatmap.stories.tsx';\n\n\n\n## Features\n\n- **Discrete color buckets**: De"},"329":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap-29","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap#examples","content":"import { ArgTypes, Meta } from '@storybook/addon-docs/blocks';\nimport { Examples } from '@bento/storybook-addon-helpers/runtime';\nimport * as Stories from './heatmap.stories.tsx';\n\n\n\n## Features\n\n- **Discrete color buckets**: Define threshold ranges with exp"},"330":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap-30","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap#custom-data-shape","content":"When your data type is not `HeatmapCell`, provide typed accessors:"},"331":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap-31","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap#sizing","content":"Cell width fills the available width. Row height has two modes, depending on whether the chart is given a height."},"332":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap-32","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap#sizing","content":"**Wrap content** (no `height`, and the parent has none): the chart is as tall as its rows. Each row is `minCellHeight` (default `32`) plus the `cellPadding` gap, with the axis and legend below. It needs no sized container, and it grows or shrinks as rows are added or removed."},"333":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap-33","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap#sizing","content":"**Fixed height** (the `height` prop, or a parent with a height): `height` is the total, including the axis and legend."},"334":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap-34","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap#sizing","content":"Rows stretch equally to fill the height."},"335":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap-35","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap#sizing","content":"Rows never go below `minCellHeight`. When they do not fit, the chart scrolls vertically and the axis labels stay pinned."},"336":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap-36","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap#sizing","content":"Set `maxCellHeight` to stop rows stretching past a size, for example a single row in a tall chart. The chart then ends after the last row, and the leftover space sits below it."},"337":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap-37","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap#sizing","content":"| Setup     | Result                                                |\n| --------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| No height | Rows at `minCellHeight`; chart is as tall as its rows |","table":"table-0"},"338":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap-38","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap#sizing","content":"| Setup                            | Result                                      |\n| -------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------- |\n| Height larger than the rows need | Rows grow to fill it, up to `maxCellHeight` |","table":"table-0"},"339":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap-39","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap#sizing","content":"| Setup                             | Result                                          |\n| --------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------- |\n| Height smaller than the rows need | Rows stay at `minCellHeight`; the chart scrolls |","table":"table-0"},"340":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap-40","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap#sizing","content":"When `maxCellHeight` leaves the chart shorter than its box, `align` chooses where it sits: `start` (default) keeps it at the top, `end` moves it to the bottom, and `center` splits the space. It has no effect when the rows fill the height."},"341":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap-41","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap#color-buckets","content":"`colorBuckets` is an ordered array of `ColorBucket` values. Each cell's fill is resolved by scanning the list and returning the first bucket where `value < bucket.max`. The last bucket should have `max: null` (open-ended); a value above every `max` also uses the last bucket. `min` is informational and is not used for matching, so list the buckets in ascending order:"},"342":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap-42","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap#closed-cells","content":"A cell with no value renders as a dashed-border rectangle with no fill. That covers `null`, `undefined` and `NaN` values, a row and column with no datum, and an empty `colorBuckets` list. Its aria role is `presentation` and it is removed from pointer and keyboard events. Use `closedLabel` to customize its legend entry (default: `\"No data\"`)."},"343":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap-43","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap#titles-and-descriptions","content":"The chart renders only the grid, axes and legend. Render titles, subtitles and date ranges in your own layout around it."},"344":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap-44","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap#legend","content":"The legend is centered below the chart, like the other chart types. Override its text per use case:"},"345":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap-45","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap#legend","content":"`colorLegendLabel`: leading label (omitted when not set)"},"346":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap-46","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap#legend","content":"`closedLabel`: entry for null cells (default `\"No data\"`)"},"347":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap-47","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap#legend","content":"`label` on each `ColorBucket`: one entry per bucket"},"348":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap-48","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap#tooltip","content":"The built-in tooltip is the same one the bar chart uses, with its arrow. It shows one row for the hovered cell: a swatch in the cell's bucket color, `{row} · {column}`, and the value (for example `● Monday · 12pm   380`)."},"349":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap-49","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap#tooltip","content":"Use `tooltipValueFormatter` to format the value, such as adding a unit:"},"350":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap-50","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap#tooltip","content":"For anything else, such as a title or a period-over-period comparison, use `renderTooltip`. It receives the hovered `datum`, so any extra field on your data (like a previous value) is available. Custom content is wrapped in the shared tooltip container and, like the other charts, has no arrow:"},"351":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap-51","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap#tooltip","content":"See the *Custom tooltip* example for a full comparison card."},"352":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap-52","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap#accessibility","content":"The `<svg>` element gets `role=\"img\"` and the `aria-label` prop"},"353":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap-53","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap#accessibility","content":"Add `desc` for a longer screen-reader description: a `<desc>` element with a unique id is injected and `aria-describedby` points to it"},"354":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap-54","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap#accessibility","content":"Each colored cell has `role=\"img\"` and an `aria-label` of `\"{row}, {column}: {value}\"`"},"355":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap-55","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap#accessibility","content":"The legend is a `role=\"list\"` labelled by `colorLegendLabel`, falling back to `\"Heatmap legend\"`"},"356":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap-56","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/heatmap#accessibility","content":"Focusing a cell with the keyboard shows its tooltip"},"357":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"page","content":"LineChart","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components","Chart"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart"},"358":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-0","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","content":"Line Chart shows how something changes over time or along a continuous scale. It connects data points with lines so people can quickly spot trends, peaks, dips, and patterns."},"359":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-1","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#installation","content":"Installation"},"360":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-2","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#examples","content":"Examples"},"361":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-3","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#customization","content":"Customization"},"362":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-4","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#data-attributes","content":"Data Attributes"},"363":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-5","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#component-customization","content":"Component Customization"},"364":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-6","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#accessibility","content":"Accessibility"},"365":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-7","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#aria-support","content":"ARIA Support"},"366":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-8","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#best-practices","content":"Best Practices"},"367":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-9","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#when-to-use-linechart","content":"When to Use LineChart"},"368":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-10","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#troubleshooting","content":"Troubleshooting"},"369":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-11","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#chart-not-sizing-or-empty","content":"Chart Not Sizing or Empty"},"370":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-12","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#dates-not-displaying-correctly","content":"Dates Not Displaying Correctly"},"371":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-13","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#tooltip-or-crosshair-not-showing","content":"Tooltip or Crosshair Not Showing"},"372":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-14","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#props","content":"Props"},"373":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-15","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#linechart","content":"LineChart"},"374":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-16","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#examples","content":"import { ArgTypes, Meta } from '@storybook/addon-docs/blocks';\nimport { Examples } from '@bento/storybook-addon-helpers/runtime';\nimport * as Stories from './line-ch"},"375":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-17","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#examples","content":"import { ArgTypes, Meta } from '@storybook/addon-docs/blocks';\nimport { Examples } from '@bento/storybook-addon-helpers/runtime';\nimport * as Stories from './line-chart.stories.tsx';\n\n<Meta of={Stories} name=\"Over"},"376":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-18","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#examples","content":"import { ArgTypes, Meta } from '@storybook/addon-docs/blocks';\nimport { Examples } from '@bento/storybook-addon-helpers/runtime';\nimport * as Stories from './line-chart.stories.tsx';\n\n\n\n##"},"377":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-19","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#examples","content":"import { ArgTypes, Meta } from '@storybook/addon-docs/blocks';\nimport { Examples } from '@bento/storybook-addon-helpers/runtime';\nimport * as Stories from './line-chart.stories.tsx';\n\n\n\n## Installation\n\n```bash"},"378":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-20","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#examples","content":"import { ArgTypes, Meta } from '@storybook/addon-docs/blocks';\nimport { Examples } from '@bento/storybook-addon-helpers/runtime';\nimport * as Stories from './line-chart.stories.tsx';\n\n\n\n## Installation\n\n```bash\nnpm"},"379":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-21","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#data-attributes","content":"The chart root exposes data attributes that reflect prop state for styling:"},"380":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-22","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#data-attributes","content":"**Chart container:** `data-width`, `data-height`, `data-x-labels`, `data-y-labels`, `data-x-labels-vertical`, `data-x-baseline`, `data-y-baseline`, `data-x-tick-marks`, `data-y-tick-marks`"},"381":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-23","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#component-customization","content":"Use the `className` prop on the chart container to add or override styles:"},"382":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-24","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#aria-support","content":"Provide **`aria-label`** to describe the chart (e.g. \"Monthly sales revenue from January to May 2024\")."},"383":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-25","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#aria-support","content":"Use **`desc`** for a longer description rendered in the SVG `<desc>` for screen readers."},"384":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-26","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#aria-support","content":"The component sets ARIA attributes on interactive and structural elements as needed."},"385":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-27","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#when-to-use-linechart","content":"Use for trends over time or along a continuous scale."},"386":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-28","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#when-to-use-linechart","content":"Use when comparing a few series (e.g. 2-5 lines); avoid too many overlapping lines."},"387":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-29","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#when-to-use-linechart","content":"Prefer a single chart with a legend over multiple small charts when comparing the same X range."},"388":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-30","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#chart-not-sizing-or-empty","content":"Ensure the chart has a non-zero size. Place it in a container with explicit dimensions or use `width` and `height`:"},"389":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-31","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#dates-not-displaying-correctly","content":"Use `xType=\"time\"` when the X-axis values are Date objects:"},"390":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-32","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#tooltip-or-crosshair-not-showing","content":"Ensure `tooltip`, `showCrosshair`, or `showDataPoints` are not set to `false`, and that the chart receives pointer events (e.g. no overlay blocking hover)."},"391":{"id":"/docs/components/checkbox","page_id":"/docs/components/checkbox","type":"page","content":"Checkbox","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/checkbox"},"392":{"id":"/docs/components/checkbox-0","page_id":"/docs/components/checkbox","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/checkbox","content":"Accessible checkbox component for multi-select options with support for indeterminate states, validation, keyboard navigation, and flexible group layouts."},"393":{"id":"/docs/components/checkbox-1","page_id":"/docs/components/checkbox","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/checkbox#installation","content":"Installation"},"394":{"id":"/docs/components/checkbox-2","page_id":"/docs/components/checkbox","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/checkbox#examples","content":"Examples"},"395":{"id":"/docs/components/checkbox-3","page_id":"/docs/components/chec