idation and disabled state"],[1593,"**Validation states**: Use `isInvalid` with a `FieldError` and `isDisabled` for validation and disabled state"],[1065,"**Value scale**: `minValue`, `maxValue`, `step`, and `formatOptions` configure the numeric behavior"],[271,"**Verify event targets**: Tooltips use mouse event coordinates and bar group positions"],[214,"**Vertical and horizontal orientations**: Choose the best layout for your data and use case"],[247,"**Vertical charts**: Horizontal scrolling when many data points exceed container width"],[223,"**VisX integration**: Leverages VisX primitives for scales, axes, shapes, and responsive layout"],[796,"**What happens with sprite mode:**"],[332,"**Wrap content** (no `height`, and the parent has none): the chart is as tall as its rows. Each row is `minCellHeight` (default `32`) plus the `cellPadding` gap, with the axis and legend below. It needs no sized container, and it grows or shrinks as rows are added or removed."],[153,"`@godaddy/antares/date` re-exports `@internationalized/date`, the package behind these date primitives."],[904,"`2xl` - 2x extra large spacing"],[680,"`acceptedFileTypes` is a best-effort filter for the OS picker — always validate file type and size again in your `onSelect` handler, since it can be bypassed."],[1236,"`aria-checked` indicates selection state"],[1357,"`aria-checked` indicates selection state"],[523,"`aria-describedby` wires the `helperText` to the progressbar for screen readers"],[435,"`aria-disabled` for disabled checkboxes"],[1237,"`aria-disabled` for disabled options"],[1358,"`aria-disabled` for disabled segments"],[437,"`aria-invalid` for validation errors"],[1239,"`aria-invalid` for validation errors"],[1689,"`aria-label` (or `aria-labelledby`) is required on the group container"],[1359,"`aria-label` required on the container for screen readers"],[522,"`aria-labelledby` associates the visible label when the `label` prop is provided"],[436,"`aria-required` when selection is required"],[1238,"`aria-required` when selection is required"],[520,"`aria-valuemin` and `aria-valuemax` define the range (default `0`–`100`)"],[519,"`aria-valuenow` is omitted while indeterminate; otherwise it reflects the current value (clamped to 0–100)"],[521,"`aria-valuetext` and visible value text are omitted while indeterminate; otherwise `aria-valuetext` provides a formatted string (e.g. `\"60%\"`) via `Intl.NumberFormat`; the same string is rendered inside the circle. Override the text with the `aria-valuetext` prop, or control formatting with `formatOptions`"],[896,"`Box` is a polymorphic layout component that renders as any HTML element or custom component via the `as` prop. It provides consistent spacing, elevation, rounding, and self-alignment within flex or grid containers."],[913,"`BoxContext` supplies default props to Boxes in its subtree. A `slots` map supplies defaults to\nnamed parts; each Box selects one with `slot`. Explicit consumer props override defaults, while\nclasses, styles, and refs are merged. Pass `slot={null}` to opt out of the context."],[560,"`Button slot=\"trigger\"` renders a native button with `aria-expanded` for its open state and\n`aria-controls` linked to the panel automatically."],[152,"`Calendar` values are `CalendarDate` objects. Import the date primitives you need from the `@godaddy/antares/date` subpath:"],[183,"`CardGroup` uses grid navigation: Tab enters or leaves, arrow keys move between Cards, and Space\nchanges selection. Enter activates row actions or links. Choose selection or `onAction`;\ncombining them prevents pointer selection."],[421,"`CheckboxGroup` is composed: write `Label`, a `Group` holding the `Checkbox` items, `Text slot=\"description\"`, and `FieldError`. The `Group` takes its axis, gap, and presentational role from the group's `orientation`, so a bare `<Group>` is all you need; pass your own `direction`/`gap` to lay the items out differently. Each `Checkbox` takes label text next to the indicator."],[482,"`C